<node id="11104685" title="Re^2: The error says the value is uninitialized, but it works anyway" created="2019-08-19 07:33:47" updated="2019-08-19 07:33:47" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;c&gt;my $x = join '|', @drop; /$x/ ? () : $_&lt;/c&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this may work for the example in the root node, it's of course pretty inefficient to build the regex on every iteration of the loop. And, the regex will match more than fixed strings, because it doesn't escape metacharacters and isn't anchored - see [id://1179840] (as has been mentioned several times already). Plus, &lt;c&gt;map { ... ? () : $_ }&lt;/c&gt; is perhaps better written as &lt;c&gt;grep { not ... }&lt;/c&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
